// Title: Code Execution via Pcwutl.dll
// Sigma ID: 9386d78a-7207-4048-9c9f-a93a7c2d1c05
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Julia Fomina, oscd.community
// Date: 2020-10-05 | Modified: 2023-02-09
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218.011
// Description: Detects launch of executable by calling the LaunchApplication function from pcwutl.dll library.
// False positives:
//   - Use of Program Compatibility Troubleshooter Helper
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Libraries/Pcwutl/
//   - https://twitter.com/harr0ey/status/989617817849876488
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_lolbin_pcwutl.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\rundll32.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "RUNDLL32.EXE") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "pcwutl" and ProcessCommandLine contains "LaunchApplication")
